ka's Senate race pairs incumbent Republican Dan Sullivan with Democrat Mary Peltola, a former congresswoman with statewide name recognition. Polls since late August have mostly shown Peltola narrowly ahead, including a New York Times/Siena survey with a seven-point lead, though several Republican-sponsored pollsters have shown Sullivan in front. Averages across firms put the race at roughly two to three points for Peltola. Outside analysts are split between calling it a tossup and a slight Democratic edge, and prediction markets price Peltola's chances around seventy percent.\n\nThe fundamentals still favor Republicans: the state leans six points right and Sullivan has won statewide before. But Peltola has outraised him substantially, the midterm environment favors her party, and Trump's October rally trip, along with voter confusion over a second Dan Sullivan on the ballot, signals concern within Republican ranks. The race sits as a narrow Democratic lean heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5747, "margin": 0.87}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6995, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6035, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5728, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6289, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6246, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.603, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6381, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6392, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6469, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6459, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6429, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6784, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0